# Dashboard versioning

The robot HMI dashboard shows a SemVer from
`src/dashboard/package.json` → Vite `__APP_VERSION__` (when wired).

This is **product UI version**, separate from fleet **Release `#N (sha)`**
(deployable robot images).

## When to bump

Bump `src/dashboard/package.json` `version` (and keep
`package-lock.json` in sync) whenever you ship an **operator-visible** change:

| Change | Bump |
|--------|------|
| New screen/feature, new columns, new API fields shown in UI | **minor** (`0.2.0` → `0.3.0`) |
| Bug fix / polish that operators can notice | **patch** (`0.3.0` → `0.3.1`) |
| Breaking dashboard UX / data model reset | **major** |

Do **not** bump for pure refactors, comments, or internal-only changes with no
UI/API surface change.

## How

1. Edit `"version"` in `src/dashboard/package.json`.
2. Update the top-level `"version"` fields in `package-lock.json` (or run
   `npm install` in `src/dashboard/`).
3. Ensure the UI picks it up via Vite `define` / footer if present.

## After bump

Robot images host the dashboard — commit, rebuild `dashboard` (+ backend when
APIs changed), publish deploy bundle, and converge the Pi via Fleet Console /
fleet-agent.
